    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Soho style revival"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Soho style revival
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening?</strong> Shaftesbury Capital has unveiled early <a href="https://www.standard.co.uk/business/sohos-carnaby-street-to-be-spruced-up-60-years-after-it-became-the-epicentre-of-the-swinging-sixties-b1274177.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">design proposals to revamp Carnaby Street</a>, one of London’s most iconic retail destinations in Soho. Proposed upgrades include softer lighting, significantly more greenery, and design elements that highlight the street’s cultural heritage from the Swinging Sixties era. The project is currently at a consultation stage, and people have been invited to provide feedback before formal planning applications are submitted to Westminster City Council.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Why?</strong> Although the street has historic cultural value dating back to the 1960s fashion boom, competition from online retail and newer shopping destinations has reduced footfall over time. Through these updates, landlords hope to encourage longer visits, increase spending, and strengthen the area’s identity as a cultural and retail hub. The project also aligns with broader urban trends supported by Westminster City Council to create greener, more walkable city centres.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>History:</strong> Carnaby Street, in London’s West End, Soho, rose to global fame during the 1960s “Swinging London” era. Independent boutiques such as Lady Jane and Lord John sold bold, modern styles that attracted celebrities, including members of The Beatles and The Rolling Stones. The street symbolised the Mod movement and Britain’s cultural revolution. After declining in the 1970s-80s, the area gradually revived through retail funding, tourism, and heritage branding.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
