<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Festival of champions"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Festival of champions
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening?</strong> The Cheltenham Festival has begun in Gloucestershire, bringing <a href="https://www.standard.co.uk/sport/horse-racing/cheltenham-festival-2026-race-card-results-winners-weather-latest-odds-day-one-b1273435.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">horse racing fans to Cheltenham Racecourse</a> for four days of top-level National Hunt racing. Running from March 10-13, 2026, the event features 28 races across four days, including highlights such as the Champion Hurdle on Tuesday and the prestigious Cheltenham Gold Cup on Friday.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Concerns: </strong>The Cheltenham Festival in 2026 is unusually unpredictable after several major contenders were ruled out before the meeting. Star horses Sir Gino and Marine Nationale will miss the festival due to injury. Former champion Constitution Hill will appear for a farewell at Cheltenham Racecourse, but will not compete as connections shift focus to flat racing. The prestigious Cheltenham Gold Cup is particularly open after Galopin Des Champs and Fact To File were ruled out
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>History:</strong> The Cheltenham Festival is one of the most prestigious events in National Hunt horse racing. The festival began in 1860 as the National Hunt Meeting and gradually evolved into a multi-day international racing event. The Cheltenham Gold Cup, first run in 1924, became its most famous contest. Over time, the festival expanded to four days with 28 races, attracting top trainers, jockeys, and horses from Britain and Ireland.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
    
<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
