    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/mar/10/england-higher-water-bills-anglian-southern-wessex-south-east" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Four major English water suppliers, Anglian Water, Southern Water, Wessex Water, and South East Water, have been allowed to raise customer bills</a> above the originally permitted level after appealing to the Competition and Markets Authority. The companies argued they needed additional revenue to fund upgrades to ageing water infrastructure such as pipes, sewers, and reservoirs. The regulator approved an average annual increase of about 2.65%.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>

