    <mj-text padding="20px 20px 10px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;">Art &amp; culture</h3>
</mj-text>
<mj-table
  font-family="Arial"
  cellpadding="0"
  cellspacing="0"
  padding="0px 32px 0px 32px"
  style="width: 100%"
>
  <tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/shopping-centre-pop-art-mural-064844597.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Eduardo Paolozzi’s large “pop art” mural inside the Kingfisher Shopping Centre has been granted Grade II listed status</a>. The mural, unveiled in 1983 in Milward Square, consists of 12 colourful mosaic panels inspired by Redditch’s historic needle-making industry. The listing was recommended by Historic England, which praised the work’s craftsmanship and cultural importance.
  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.houghtonhall.com/whats-on/lynn-chadwick-at-houghton-hall" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Houghton Hall will host a major sculpture exhibition dedicated to Lynn Chadwick beginning 2 May 2026</a>. The exhibition will present around 30 works spanning four decades of Chadwick’s career, from the 1950s to the 1990s. Curated by Pangolin London, the show will feature artworks placed throughout the estate's interiors and outdoor grounds. It will be the largest UK exhibition of Chadwick’s work in more than twenty years, following the retrospective held at Tate Britain in 2003.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>
<mj-text padding="20px 20px 10px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <h3 style="font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;">Sports</h3>
</mj-text>
<mj-table
  font-family="Arial"
  cellpadding="0"
  cellspacing="0"
  padding="0px 32px 0px 32px"
  style="width: 100%"
>
  <tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/cricket/the-hundred-auction-players-time-tv-channel-tickets-b2935487.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">The Hundred will hold its first-ever player auction this week, replacing the previous draft system used since the tournament’s launch</a>. Organised by the England and Wales Cricket Board, this format allows franchises to bid competitively for players rather than selecting them in turns. The change mirrors the auction model used in the Indian Premier League and follows increased funding from IPL franchise owners.
  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td style="
    font-size: 18px;
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  "> &#8226; </td>
  <td style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    padding-left: 0px;
  ">
    <a href="https://talksport.com/football/4038742/tottenham-transfers-summer-firesale-romero-van-de-ven/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">Tottenham Hotspur is reportedly planning a major squad overhaul over the next three transfer windows as part of a long-term rebuild</a>. The club is prepared to sell most of its current players this summer to fund signings, with just nine members of the squad expected to be retained. Among those potentially leaving is vice-captain Cristian Romero, despite signing an agreement last year.
  </td>
</tr>
</mj-table>
